BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:state-sales-iowa-q1-2025-02-28@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250228
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250301
SUMMARY:Iowa: State sales & use tax return due
DESCRIPTION:Iowa's sales/use tax filing frequency is NOT quarterly - confir
 med directly against the Iowa Administrative Code (701-202.1(423)\, publish
 ed by the Iowa Legislature at legis.iowa.gov\, the state's own official cod
 ification): "A retailer owing $1\,200 or more in sales or use tax per calen
 dar year shall file a sales and use tax return once per month. This monthly
  return is due on or before the last day of the month following the end of 
 the month in which the tax was collected. A retailer owing less than $1\,20
 0 in sales or use tax per calendar year shall file a sales and use tax retu
 rn at least once per annual year\, due on or before January 31 for the prio
 r calendar year." The four dates below are representative monthly due dates
  (last day of the following month) spread across 2026 for the standard $1\,
 200-or-more monthly filer\, not literal calendar quarters - Iowa has no qua
 rterly sales tax filing option under current rule. Small filers under the $
 1\,200 annual threshold instead file once a year\, by January 31. | Monthly
  return for January 2026 sales\, due the last day of February 2026 (illustr
 ative monthly occurrence). Iowa's sales/use tax filing frequency is NOT qua
 rterly - confirmed directly against the Iowa Administrative Code (701-202.1
 (423)\, published by the Iowa Legislature at legis.iowa.gov\, the state's o
 wn official codification): "A retailer owing $1\,200 or more in sales or us
 e tax per calendar year shall file a sales and use tax return once per mont
 h. This monthly return is due on or before the last day of the month follow
 ing the end of the month in which the tax was collected. A retailer owing l
 ess than $1\,200 in sales or use tax per calendar year shall file a sales a
 nd use tax return at least once per annual year\, due on or before January 
 31 for the prior calendar year." The four dates below are representative mo
 nthly due dates (last day of the following month) spread across 2026 for th
 e standard $1\,200-or-more monthly filer\, not literal calendar quarters - 
 Iowa has no quarterly sales tax filing option under current rule. Small fil
 ers under the $1\,200 annual threshold instead file once a year\, by Januar
 y 31. | Authority: Iowa Administrative Code 701-202.1(423)\, official codif
 ication published by the Iowa Legislature (legis.iowa.gov) | Source: https:
 //www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/701.202.pdf | This date is computed f
 rom a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confir
 m against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
