 ed by the Iowa Legislature at legis.iowa.gov\, the state's own official cod
 ification): "A retailer owing $1\,200 or more in sales or use tax per calen
 dar year shall file a sales and use tax return once per month. This monthly
  return is due on or before the last day of the month following the end of 
 the month in which the tax was collected. A retailer owing less than $1\,20
 0 in sales or use tax per calendar year shall file a sales and use tax retu
 rn at least once per annual year\, due on or before January 31 for the prio
 r calendar year." The four dates below are representative monthly due dates
  (last day of the following month) spread across 2026 for the standard $1\,
 200-or-more monthly filer\, not literal calendar quarters - Iowa has no qua
 rterly sales tax filing option under current rule. Small filers under the $
 1\,200 annual threshold instead file once a year\, by January 31. | Monthly
